    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώρ-ισμα</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that by which a thing is made
				known, mark, token</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.1.27
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Phgn.</u>
				806a15
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴχνη καὶ γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.855b
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <i>tokens by which</i> a lost child <i>is
				recognized</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, etc.: also in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				1.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in criminal
			trials, <i>corpus delicti,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PMasp.
				143.16
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>.</div>
